  M4 CANDIDATE [D-talk-request henry_zhang turns=11 naturalEnd=true]:
    NPC: "You told me yes, once. No details. I haven't forgotten. I just don't ask."
    NPC: "Help me haul something back? Too much for one."
    YOU: "All right. Let's go."
    NPC: You walk to the cache spot with Henry. Nothing much there — but they talk the whole way, and you learn the shape of them a little better.
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "that personal stuff — that's still where we are."
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: Something in them stays shut, for now.
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: A beat. Then, as if shaking something off:
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: "Are you angry? At whoever did this. At the sky. At anything."
    YOU: "Furious. Most days."
    NPC: "Good. Anger's fuel. Just — point it somewhere useful."
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: "Anger's a fire — useful if you cook with it, deadly if you sleep next to it. I cook with mine. Most days."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "We're going in circles — still on that personal stuff. Ask me something else if you want."
    YOU: "Want to come with us?"
    NPC: "Okay. Yeah. I trust you."
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: "Okay. We'll pick this up later."
    YOU: "..."
    NPC: You say nothing. Neither do they, for a while — and it's fine.
    NPC: "...Think about it? I'll be around."
    NPC: "Good — that personal stuff, settled. Feels better said out loud."
    NPC: They're smiling as you go. "Come back anytime."

